From 4b881648c70953a80af76adf410eb8c2799ae832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fabian <fabian.maass@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Dec 2025 21:33:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(requests): add auto-delete scheduling with blocklist
 integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add auto-delete field to MediaRequest entity (nullable datetime column)
- Create scheduled job to delete expired media daily at 3:00 AM
- Support configurable retention periods: 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180 days
- Add auto-delete option in movie request modal UI
- Create AutoDeleteBlock component with visual progress bar and countdown display
- Display auto-delete status in manage panel with set/cancel controls
- Show inline auto-delete indicator with clock icon in request lists
- Auto-deleted items automatically added to blocklist (tag: 'auto-deleted')
- Supports both APPROVED and COMPLETED request statuses
- API: POST/GET /api/v1/request/auto-delete/:requestId
- Manual job trigger: POST /api/v1/settings/jobs/auto-delete-expired/run
- Database migrations for SQLite and PostgreSQL

Technical implementation:
- AutoDeleteExpired job queries expired requests and deletes from Radarr/Sonarr
- Deletion includes files (deleteFiles: true) and adds to blocklist
- Blocklist integration prevents re-requesting via list sync jobs
- UI uses cache-busting page reload (window.location + timestamp) for fresh data
- OpenAPI spec updated with auto-delete endpoint definitions
- Job registered in scheduler with cron: '0 0 3 * * *' (3 AM daily)
- MediaRequest.request() accepts autoDeleteDays parameter for immediate scheduling
- Approval endpoint enhanced to accept autoDeleteAfterDays for post-approval scheduling

Depends-on: feat(blacklist): 2-way blocklist sync (for Blacklist.addToBlacklist)

Test:
- Request movie → Set auto-delete 90 days → Gear icon → Manage panel shows countdown
- API test: curl -X POST /api/v1/request/auto-delete/ID -d '{"days": 90}'
- Manual trigger: curl -X POST /api/v1/settings/jobs/auto-delete-expired/run
